{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The 5.00 SGD is already out of the rider's hands: EV-FARE-05067 records payment_status REFUNDED with refund_issued_sgd 5.00, and the trip record shows the fee reversed to the rider and withheld from the driver at 2026-09-13T10:46:10+08:00. Under POL-GEN-03 the driver's filing has to be read against that present payment state - NO_ACTION preserves the present state and never means 'restore a charge' - so the driver must affirmatively make out an entitlement to the whole 5.00 SGD before any money moves back to him. That is the frame for every point below.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05067", "EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider does not dispute the driver's contact: EV-CHAT-05067 carries three in-app messages from the driver (09:22:00, 09:25:30, 09:28:40) and EV-TRIP-05067 carries two in-app calls placed by the driver (09:24:10 and 09:27:20), all before the 09:30:10 cancellation. POL-NS-23's chat-and-call obligation is therefore met and the rider's case does not rest on it. What the rider's case rests on is this trip's timing, which the record cannot supply at all.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05067", "EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This booking has no scheduled pickup time: trip_record.scheduled_at is null in EV-TRIP-05067 and the derived driver_deadline is null with the reason 'on-demand trip: no scheduled time'. POL-NS-24 measures the driver's punctuality from the scheduled time plus 5 minutes, and its own note directs that where the record carries none and the deadline cannot be fixed, POL-GEN-26 applies; no artifact in this package can fix it. The timing fact that limb of the no-show framework needs is therefore not established on this record, and POL-GEN-26 sends the case to a human reviewer with the amount held - which leaves the 5.00 SGD refunded to the rider where it is, rather than paying it over to the driver on a deadline nobody can compute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.scheduled_at",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The no-show conclusion rests on the platform's wait timer and nothing else. EV-GPS-05067 carries an empty rider track (rider_track: []) and no rider-presence block, so no artifact places the rider anywhere; nothing in the record corroborates or contradicts her account that she was downstairs waiting, and the driver's own messages in EV-CHAT-05067 never once state that she was absent - his 09:25:30 message says he was himself 'waiting downstairs'. Whether the rider was at the pickup and available is a fact the record cannot establish either way, and POL-GEN-26 does not allow that gap to be filled by inference against her.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-05067", "EV-CHAT-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.rider_track",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's profile carries fraud_flags 3. I cite that field for one purpose only and for the rule that names it - POL-GEN-22, carried into no-shows by POL-NS-26 - and never as a fact about this trip (POL-GEN-01). Its effect is concrete: the confidence an AI ruling must reach on this dispute is 0.95, not the 'any confidence' that a 5.00 SGD no-show would otherwise bear. On a record whose only rider-side material is the rider's own uncorroborated note, and which cannot fix the trip's timing at all, a money ruling for the driver should not be issued at that bar; the fee should stay held for review.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.fraud_flags",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "EV-ADVIS-05067-01 is MISSING - no traffic record was attached for this trip - so it has no payload and an admissibility weight of 0.0, and I cite it at that weight and put no fact on it. Its absence means nothing on the record explains the 385 s the driver took between acceptance (09:15:20) and the arrival event (09:21:45) over a traced 1.444 km (EV-GPS-05067). Under POL-GEN-02 a MISSING artifact carries no fact and caps nothing by itself; under POL-GEN-26 a record with a hole this size in the trip's circumstances is one for review rather than for a money ruling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-05067-01", "EV-GPS-05067", "EV-TRIP-05067"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02", "POL-GEN-26"],
      "relies_on": "evidence.EV-ADVIS-05067-01.admissibility.weight_multiplier",
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 5.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 5.0,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties: on 13 Sep 2026 the platform charged the rider a 5.00 SGD no-show fee and then, after her complaint, reversed it to her and withheld it from the driver 'pending review'. The driver has filed asking for that sum back. On this record the fee was correctly charged and the driver is owed the 5.00 SGD.\n\nThe driver's arrival at Block 680 is established, not merely asserted. The trip record (EV-TRIP-05067, weight 1.0) puts arrival at 09:21:45, and the driver's GPS trace (EV-GPS-05067, weight 1.0) corroborates it: the nearest fix is 1.81 m from the pickup, reporting 6 m accuracy, inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD zone (POL-NS-21). Under POL-NS-21 the 300-second free wait runs from that arrival, scheduled trip or not, so it expired at 09:26:45; the cancellation at 09:30:10 came 505 seconds after arrival, i.e. after the free wait. The driver's contact obligation (POL-NS-23) was also met: three in-app messages (09:22:00, 09:25:30, 09:28:40) and two in-app calls (09:24:10, 09:27:20), every one before the 09:30:10 cancellation. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-05067, weight 1.0) shows a single 5.00 SGD cancellation-fee line, matching POL-NS-22's fixed 5.00 SGD no-show fee. The fee therefore stands under POL-NS-22; because the platform has already moved 5.00 SGD back to the rider, that same 5.00 SGD is now returned to the driver: DRIVER_COMPENSATION, with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00.\n\nThe rider's points are answered. She is right, and it is not in dispute, that POL-NS-23's chat-and-call obligation was met. She is right that POL-GEN-03 reads the driver's filing against the present payment state, but the driver has affirmatively made out his entitlement to the whole 5.00 SGD, so that frame leaves the money with him rather than with the interim refund. Her argument that POL-NS-24 and POL-GEN-26 send this to a human reviewer fails: POL-NS-24 gives the rider a right to cancel without charge when the driver is late for a scheduled pickup, and she never cancelled; and the free wait on an on-demand trip runs from the driver's arrival (POL-NS-21, settled by Ryde on 14 Oct 2026), so no scheduled time is needed to decide this fee and POL-GEN-26 is not engaged. Her further argument that the record cannot place her at the pickup does not engage POL-GEN-26 either, because no rule makes the rider's own location an element of the fee; the fee turns on the driver's arrival, wait and contact, all established. Her statement that the driver 'never came to my block' is contradicted by the GPS trace, which shows the vehicle stationary at the pickup from 09:21:50 through 09:29:50, and nothing on the record corroborates her account (the rider track is empty). Finally, the rider's profile carries a fraud flag (3), which under POL-GEN-22 and POL-NS-26 raises the confidence this ruling needs to 0.95; every artifact carrying the deciding facts is COMPLETE at weight 1.0 (POL-GEN-02(2)), so the ruling is issued at exactly 0.95. No referral is produced: the fee charged (5.00 SGD) is exactly POL-NS-22's fee, so no fee-amount referral arises, and the rider's no-show count of 1, even adding this trip, stays below POL-NS-25's threshold of 3."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
